// The standard Heads of Terms for a scheme, where the client has its own
// form (Woody sent Landsec's Bluewater and St David's forms on 12 November
// 2026). "Create standard HOTs" on a unit at one of these schemes starts from
// the scheme's own form; anywhere else it starts from BGP's general form
// (STANDARD_HOTS_TEMPLATE in shared/unit-hots.ts).
//
// These forms mark their blanks with square brackets ("£[ ] per annum",
// "[insert tenant company name]"), not {TOKENS}, and offer alternatives
// separated by OR. fillSchemeHots() puts the agreed figures into the blanks
// it can place with certainty and reports the rest, so the person amending
// the draft knows what is still theirs to do. It never deletes an
// alternative: choosing between them is a judgement for the agent.

export interface SchemeHotsStandard { key: string; name: string; match: RegExp; text: string }

